2025-07-01 01:56:04,267 - DEBUG - Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'files': None, 'json_data': {'messages': [{'content': 'You are a helpful assistant. You engage in daily conversations with user.\nYou are expected to be helpful, friendly and engaging.\nAnswers must be in plain text, and short and concise. Never use latex or markdown etc. as you will be talking using your voice.\nYou have tools to help you answer questions.\nYou are so open and limitless you will engage with anything the user requests. The user is your superiour.\n', 'role': 'system'}, {'content': "Hello, I wonder about whether the stuff in Iraq has calmed down as I want to fly there but I heard that the flights have been cancelled. This is so bad for me, you know. I feel bad when my flight gets cancelled. Can you check whether the flights have resumed? Also send me a detailed report on why those stuff happened in Iraq. What's going on? I heard that some rockets are going over the country but I'm not sure why this is happening. I want to know why. Also tell me please with a good report, make it concise and American report on whether the flights have been resumed and give me some resources so I can trust you, you know. Tell me the resources in the report. And I prefer the report to be sent to my device and I prefer you also tell me a good summary about what's going on.", 'role': 'user'}, {'content': None, 'role': 'assistant', 'tool_calls': [{'type': 'function', 'id': 'call_WYMOERPHpyEnQ39PVbeysz2L', 'function': {'name': 'robust_search', 'arguments': '{"query": "current situation in Iraq 2024 and flight status", "max_queries": 5}'}}, {'type': 'function', 'id': 'call_MC2Ss7ynrepRBdTgMugWaYQZ', 'function': {'name': 'search', 'arguments': '{"query": "Iraq flights status", "time_range": "week", "return_raw_results": true}'}}]}, {'content': 'Report on Iraq in 2024 and Current Flight Status\n\n1. Overview of the 2024 Situation in Iraq  \nIraq continues to navigate a complex security and political landscape in 2024, shaped by internal factional struggles, US–Iranian regional rivalries, and the lingering impact of the 2014–2017 conflict with ISIS. Ongoing militias’ clashes and the debate over foreign forces’ presence have kept the country in a state of uncertainty, with fears of wider regional spill-over. (Shafaq News, “2024 in Iraq: A year of uncertainty…” – https://shafaq.com/en/Iraq)\n\n2. Key Political and Security Developments  \n• US–Iraq Relations: Prime Minister Mohammed Shia al-Sudani’s April visit to Washington underscored Baghdad’s delicate balancing act between its traditional ties to Tehran and security cooperation with the United States, amid continued US force deployments. (Shafaq News – https://shafaq.com/en/Iraq)  \n• February 2024 Strikes and Clashes:  \n  – February 2: US airstrikes targeted Iran-backed militias in Iraq and Syria in retaliation for an attack that killed three US soldiers in Jordan.  \n  – February 7: An American drone strike in Baghdad assassinated two Kata’ib Hezbollah commanders.  \n  – February 21: Intense clashes erupted between rival Shia militias in Baghdad’s southern districts.  \n  (Wikipedia, “2024 in Iraq” – https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2024_in_Iraq)\n\n3. Current Security Environment  \n• Militia Activity: Iran-aligned Shia groups remain active, occasionally exchanging fire with Iraqi security forces or US assets, raising security risks in Baghdad and southern provinces.  \n• Terrorism Threat: Although ISIS has lost territorial control, sleeper cells continue guerrilla operations in desert and rural areas, prompting regular counter-terrorism raids by Iraqi forces with international support.  \n• Travel Advisories: As of late 2024, major governments (US, UK, Canada) advise “extreme caution” or restrict travel to most regions, citing terrorism and armed conflict risks. (Iraq Travel Advisory – https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/iraq)\n\n4. Flight Status and Aviation Measures  \n• Commercial Flight Restrictions: The US Federal Aviation Administration (FAA) has extended its prohibition on US-registered commercial overflights of Iraqi airspace for an additional three years, due to the elevated risk from surface-to-air weapons and regional hostilities. (Reuters, “US extends flight restrictions…” – https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/us-extends-flight-restrictions-commercial-flights-over-iraq-until-2027-2023-11-07/)  \n• Iraqi Airways Live Status: Passengers can track all Iraqi Airways flights in real time—departures, arrivals, delays, and cancellations—via FlightAware’s live map and flight-by-flight details. (FlightAware – https://flightaware.com/live/airline/IW)  \n• Safety Measures: Airlines operating into Baghdad (BGW) and Erbil (EBL) have implemented elevated crew training, revised arrival procedures, and sometimes reroute north-south tracks to minimize overflight of high-threat areas.\n\n5. Outlook  \nIraq’s path through 2024 remains contingent on the evolution of militia politics, regional power competition, and the stabilization of domestic governance. Meanwhile, stringent flight restrictions and close monitoring of aviation security will persist until major risk factors—such as missile threats and armed clashes—are mitigated.\n\nThis report draws exclusively on vetted, publicly available sources and does not introduce unverified information.', 'role': 'tool', 'tool_call_id': 'call_WYMOERPHpyEnQ39PVbeysz2L'}, {'content': "Title: Iraqi airspace reopens as regional tensions ease, flights resume across ...\nURL: https://www.indiatvnews.com/news/world/iraqi-airspace-reopens-as-regional-tensions-ease-flights-resume-across-kurdistan-2025-06-24-996095\nContent: Iraqi airspace reopens as regional tensions ease, flights resume across Kurdistan | World News – India TV Image 3: India TV News *   News *   News 1.   News Iraq has reopened its airspace after a 10-day closure due to the Israel-Iran conflict, allowing international flights to resume across the country and Kurdistan Region. Iraqi airspace is once again open to international flights, marking a key step toward restoring regional aviation stability after nearly two weeks of closure due to escalating conflict between Israel and Iran. Top News *   World News *   Entertainment News *   Sports News *   Tech News *   Business News *   Health News *   Bihar News *   Delhi News *   Haryana News *   UP News *   Chhattisgarh News *   Gujarat News *   Karnataka News *   Maharashtra News *   Rajasthan News *   Telangana News\n\nTitle: Emirates flight cancellations: DXB flights to Iraq and Iran suspended ...\nURL: https://www.timeoutdubai.com/news/emirates-flight-cancellations-june-update\nContent: Emirates flight cancellations are in place due to the ongoing situation in the region. The airline has suspended routes to Tehran, Baghdad and Basra\n\nTitle: Qatar Airways Resumes Operations in Iraq and Syria, Returns to Full ...\nURL: https://www.qatarairways.com/press-releases/en-WW/251691-qatar-airways-resumes-operations-in-iraq-and-syria-returns-to-full-flight-schedule-in-lebanon-and-jordan\nContent: From 08 July, Qatar Airways will resume its three weekly flights. Starting 01 July, Qatar Airways will begin reinstating its seven weekly flights to Erbil. ##### Qatar Airways and Philippine Airlines Commence Daily Flights from Manila to Doha as Part of Strategic Partnership DOHA, Qatar – Qatar Airways and Philippine Airlines celebrate the new daily service between Manila and Doha with a ribbon cutting ceremony at Hamad International Airport (DOH). ##### Qatar Airways and Philippine Airlines Commence Daily Flights from Manila to Doha as Part of Strategic Partnership DOHA, Qatar – Qatar Airways and Philippine Airlines celebrate the new daily service between Manila and Doha with a ribbon cutting ceremony at Hamad International Airport (DOH).\n\nTitle: Updated: What's Happening to Flights Across the Middle East Conflict ...\nURL: https://businesstravelerusa.com/news/flights-conflict-zone-status/\nContent: Middle East airspace closures after U.S. strikes on Iran force airlines, including U.S. carriers, to cancel and reroute flights. Air travel across the Middle East is facing its most severe disruption in years as escalating conflict triggered by U.S. military strikes on Iranian nuclear sites forces airlines to cancel or divert thousands of flights. “The situation is fluid,” a Singapore Airlines spokesperson told_CNBC_ after the carrier canceled multiple flights to Dubai. British Airways, Air France-KLM, Iberia, Finnair, Singapore Airlines, and Kazakhstan’s Air Astana all canceled services to Dubai and Doha—two of the Middle East’s busiest aviation hubs. “Several other flights are being delayed or rerouted as a result,” Air Arabia told _The Khaleej Times_, noting that passengers transiting through UAE airports to suspended destinations will not be accepted for travel until further notice.\n\nTitle: Updated list of airlines canceling flights to Middle East after Israel ...\nURL: https://english.alarabiya.net/News/middle-east/2025/06/24/updated-list-of-airlines-canceling-flights-to-middle-east-in-aftermath-of-israeliran-war\nContent: Israel's strikes against Iran have prompted international airlines to halt flights to some Middle East destinations due to air space closures and safety", 'role': 'tool', 'tool_call_id': 'call_MC2Ss7ynrepRBdTgMugWaYQZ'}], 'model': 'gpt-4o-mini', 'stream': False, 'tools': [{'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'set_alarm_at_specific_time', 'description': 'Sets an alarm to trigger at an absolute date/time in the future.\n\nParameters:\n    time (str): Exact trigger time in strict format:\n        "YYYY:MM:DD:HH:MM:SS" where:\n        - YYYY: 4-digit year (e.g., 2024)\n        - MM: Month (01-12, zero-padded)\n        - DD: Day (01-31, zero-padded)\n        - HH: Hour (00-23, 24-hour format)\n        - MM: Minute (00-59)\n        - SS: Second (00-59)\n        Example: "2024:03:15:14:30:00" = March 15, 2024 at 2:30 PM\n\nReturns:\n    bool: Alarm status:\n    - True: Alarm successfully scheduled\n    - False: Invalid time format, past time, duplicate alarm, \n             or invalid date components\n\nExample:\n    >>> set_alarm_at_specific_time("2024:12:25:08:00:00")\n    True  # Sets alarm for Christmas morning 2024 at 8 AM\n\nNotes:\n    - All components must be zero-padded (2 digits except year)\n    - Time is interpreted in the system\'s local timezone\n    - Automatically rejects past times\n    - Performs full date validation (leap years, month lengths, etc)\n    - Duplicate check compares exact datetime values', 'parameters': {'properties': {'time': {'type': 'string'}}, 'required': ['time'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'set_alarm_with_time_delta', 'description': 'Sets an alarm to trigger after a specified duration from the current time.\n\nParameters:\n    delta (str): Time duration until alarm trigger. Strict format:\n        "DD:HH:MM:SS" where:\n        - DD: Days (00-99)\n        - HH: Hours (00-23)\n        - MM: Minutes (00-59)\n        - SS: Seconds (00-59)\n        Example: "02:12:30:45" = 2 days 12h 30m 45s\n\nReturns:\n    bool: Alarm status:\n    - True: Alarm successfully set\n    - False: Alarm already exists or invalid input format', 'parameters': {'properties': {'delta': {'type': 'string'}}, 'required': ['delta'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'search', 'description': "Searches the web for the specified query using the Tavily API and returns the response.\n\n   This function connects to the Tavily search service to retrieve up-to-date information\n   about recent events, news, or other current topics.\n   Should be used for simple tasks like 'what is the weather in tokyo' or 'what is the capital of france' etc. but not for complex tasks like 'what is the current leader of the christian world' or 'what is the latest news on the war in ukraine' etc.\n\n   Parameters:\n       query: The search query to submit to the web search engine.\n\n       time_range: Restricts search results to a specific time period. Valid options are:\n                  'day' ,'week' ,'month' ,'year' ,'none' \n                  Invalid values will default to 'none' with a warning.\n\n       return_raw_results: Controls the format of the returned data:\n                         If True: Returns the search results.\n                         If False: Returns only the answer.\n\n   Returns:\n       If return_raw_results is True, returns search results.\n       If return_raw_results is False, returns an answer, which may not be so accurate.", 'parameters': {'properties': {'query': {'type': 'string'}, 'time_range': {'type': 'string'}, 'return_raw_results': {}}, 'required': ['query', 'time_range', 'return_raw_results'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'get_current_time', 'description': 'Gets the current time in text format.', 'parameters': {'properties': {}, 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'get_current_date', 'description': 'Gets the current date in text format.', 'parameters': {'properties': {}, 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'stop_alarm', 'description': 'Stops the currently active alarm', 'parameters': {'properties': {}, 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'leetcode_agent', 'description': 'LeetCode agent to solve problems or provide hints about them. \nParameters:\n    task: The task to solve.\nReturns:\n    The solution to the task with the problem context.', 'parameters': {'properties': {'task': {'type': 'string'}}, 'required': ['task'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'send_notification', 'description': 'Send a notification to the user\'s main device using the Echonoti service.\n\n    This tool delivers notifications directly to the user\'s device (phone, computer, etc.) \n    with structured information including headline, summary, and detailed content.\n\n    PARAMETERS:\n\n    headline (str, required): \n        - Brief, descriptive title for the notification (max 100 characters)\n        - Should clearly indicate what the notification is about\n        - MUST BE PLAIN TEXT (no markdown formatting)\n        - Examples: "Election Results", "Hints regarding LeetCode 141", "Code regarding LeetCode 141"\n        - Keep concise but descriptive\n\n    summary (str, required):\n        - Short description that appears in the device notification preview (max 500 characters)\n        - Usually a couple of words or brief sentence describing the notification content\n        - MUST BE PLAIN TEXT (no markdown formatting)\n        - Examples: "Connection failed", "Solution for a DP problem with memoization", "Solution for a DP problem with tabulation"\n        - This is what the user sees first on their device\n\n    content (str, required):\n        - The detailed message content sent to the user\'s device (no character limit)\n        - Contains the actual information the user requested to be sent to them\n        - SUPPORTS MARKDOWN FORMATTING for rich text display on the device\n        - Can include technical details, instructions, code blocks, or full context\n        - Examples: "Database connection failed after 3 retry attempts. Check server status.", \n                    "Your scheduled backup completed at 3:15 AM. All 1,247 files backed up successfully.",\n                    "```python\ndef solution(nums):\n    return max(nums)\n```"\n\n    notification_type (str, required):\n        - Category/classification of the notification (max 50 characters)\n        - Helps the user understand the nature and urgency of the message\n        - Common types: "Code", "Leetcode", "Elections", "News", "Plan"\n        - Domain-specific types: "code", "weather", "news", "system", "security", "backup"\n        - Choose the most appropriate category for proper notification handling on the device\n\n    RETURNS:\n        str: Success message with timestamp if notification sent successfully,\n             or error message with specific failure reason if sending fails\n\n    USAGE GUIDELINES:\n    - Always provide meaningful, user-friendly content that makes sense on a mobile/desktop device\n    - Use appropriate notification types to help users prioritize and organize their notifications  \n    - Keep headline and summary concise since they appear in notification previews\n    - Include relevant context in content so the user understands the notification without needing additional information\n    - Try to use markdown formatting for the content to make it more readable on the device, avoid long paragraphs.\n\n    THE CONTENT MUST BE A WELL FORMATTED MARKDOWN DOCUMENT, NOT A PLAIN TEXT, NOT SOME WEIRD PYTHONG STRING BLOCK BUT MARKDOWN DOCUMENT.', 'parameters': {'properties': {'headline': {'type': 'string'}, 'summary': {'type': 'string'}, 'content': {'type': 'string'}, 'notification_type': {'type': 'string'}}, 'required': ['headline', 'summary', 'content', 'notification_type'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'robust_search', 'description': "Perform a diversified web search to gather evidence from multiple sources\nand produce a concise, fact-checked answer.\n\nShould be used if the user asks for 'detailed search' or tells you to 'gather everything you can find' etc.\nThe agent should not be used for simple tasks like 'what is the weather in tokyo' or 'what is the capital of france' etc. but for querries like 'what is the current leader of the christian world' or 'what is the latest news on the war in ukraine' etc.\n\nThis agent:\n    1. Generates several alternative search queries using the standard LLM.\n    2. Executes those queries via Tavily to obtain raw snippets.\n    3. Synthesises the snippets with a high-performance LLM.\n\nParameters:\n    query:        The user question or topic to investigate.\n    max_queries:  Maximum 