onflict-zone-status/\nContent: Middle East airspace closures after U.S. strikes on Iran force airlines, including U.S. carriers, to cancel and reroute flights. Air travel across the Middle East is facing its most severe disruption in years as escalating conflict triggered by U.S. military strikes on Iranian nuclear sites forces airlines to cancel or divert thousands of flights. “The situation is fluid,” a Singapore Airlines spokesperson told_CNBC_ after the carrier canceled multiple flights to Dubai. British Airways, Air France-KLM, Iberia, Finnair, Singapore Airlines, and Kazakhstan’s Air Astana all canceled services to Dubai and Doha—two of the Middle East’s busiest aviation hubs. “Several other flights are being delayed or rerouted as a result,” Air Arabia told _The Khaleej Times_, noting that passengers transiting through UAE airports to suspended destinations will not be accepted for travel until further notice.\n\nTitle: Updated list of airlines canceling flights to Middle East after Israel ...\nURL: https://english.alarabiya.net/News/middle-east/2025/06/24/updated-list-of-airlines-canceling-flights-to-middle-east-in-aftermath-of-israeliran-war\nContent: Israel's strikes against Iran have prompted international airlines to halt flights to some Middle East destinations due to air space closures and safety", 'role': 'tool', 'tool_call_id': 'call_MC2Ss7ynrepRBdTgMugWaYQZ'}, {'content': None, 'role': 'assistant', 'tool_calls': [{'type': 'function', 'id': 'call_Ro6x1B2CIEbxN4WbyCaKyrTK', 'function': {'name': 'send_notification', 'arguments': '{"headline": "Iraq Flight Status and Situation Report", "summary": "Latest updates on flights to Iraq and the security situation", "content": "**Report on Iraq in 2024 and Current Flight Status**  \\n1. **Overview of the 2024 Situation in Iraq**  \\nIraq continues to navigate a complex security and political landscape in 2024, shaped by internal factional struggles, US\\u2013Iranian regional rivalries, and the lingering impact of the 2014\\u20132017 conflict with ISIS. Ongoing clashes and the debate over foreign forces\\u2019 presence have kept the country uncertain.  (Shafaq News \\u2013 https://shafaq.com/en/Iraq)  \\n\\n2. **Current Security Environment**  \\n- **Militia Activity:** Iranian-aligned Shia groups remain active, posing security risks in Baghdad and southern provinces.  \\n- **Terrorism Threat:** Despite ISIS losing control of territory, sleeper cells continue to operate.  \\n- **Travel Advisories:** Major governments advise \\u201cextreme caution\\u201d or restrict travel to most regions (Iraq Travel Advisory \\u2013 https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/iraq).  \\n\\n3. **Flight Status and Aviation Measures**  \\n- **Commercial Flight Restrictions:** The US FAA extended its prohibition on US-registered flights over Iraqi airspace, citing the elevated risk from armed conflict (Reuters \\u2013 https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/us-extends-flight-restrictions-commercial-flights-over-iraq-until-2027-2023-11-07/).  \\n- **Flight Resumption:** Iraqi airspace has reopened to international flights after a closure due to regional tensions related to the Israel-Iran conflict, allowing flights to resume across Iraq (India TV \\u2013 https://www.indiatvnews.com/news/world/iraqi-airspace-reopens-as-regional-tensions-ease-flights-resume-across-kurdistan-2025-06-24-996095).  \\n\\n4. **Outlook**  \\nIraq\\u2019s future in 2024 depends on militia politics and regional power dynamics, with ongoing flight restrictions and heightened aviation security continuing as long as risks persist.\\n\\nFor detailed, trustworthy updates, refer to the sources cited within this report.\\n\\n**Sources:**  \\n- Shafaq News  \\n- Wikipedia  \\n- Iraq Travel Advisory  \\n- Reuters  \\n- India TV", "notification_type": "News"}'}}]}, {'content': 'Successfully sent notification to the device with echonoti. Time of notification: 2025-06-30T22:56:14.893Z.', 'role': 'tool', 'tool_call_id': 'call_Ro6x1B