` characters of the string match the first `j` characters of the pattern.\\n2. **Initialize**: Set `dp[0][0]` to `true` (empty string matches empty pattern). Initialize rows for the pattern based on leading asterisks.\\n3. **Fill the Table**: Iterate through both the string and the pattern:\\n   - If characters match or the pattern has `?`, inherit the diagonal value from `dp[i-1][j-1]`.\\n   - If the pattern has `*`, check two situations (matching zero characters or some characters).\\n4. **Final Check**: Return the value at `dp[s_len][p_len]` where `s_len` and `p_len` are the lengths of the string and pattern, respectively.\\n\\n### Example:\\nInput: `s = \\"aa\\"`, `p = \\"a*\\"`  \\nOutput: `true`\\n\\nThis means the pattern matches the string successfully!", "notification_type": "LeetCode"}'}}]}, {'content': 'Successfully sent notification to the device with echonoti. Time of notification: 2025-06-30T22:58:07.425Z.', 'role': 'tool', 'tool_call_id': 'call_KIkevtrtJcgSkeqJ64EM9EWv'}], 'model': 'gpt-4o-mini', 'stream': False, 'tools': [{'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'set_alarm_at_specific_time', 'description': 'Sets an alarm to trigger at an absolute date/time in the future.\n\nParameters:\n    time (str): Exact trigger time in strict format:\n        "YYYY:MM:DD:HH:MM:SS" where:\n        - YYYY: 4-digit year (e.g., 2024)\n        - MM: Month (01-12, zero-padded)\n        - DD: Day (01-31, zero-padded)\n        - HH: Hour (00-23, 24-hour format)\n        - MM: Minute (00-59)\n        - SS: Second (00-59)\n        Example: "2024:03:15:14:30:00" = March 15, 2024 at 2:30 PM\n\nReturns:\n    bool: Alarm status:\n    - True: Alarm successfully scheduled\n    - False: Invalid time format, past time, duplicate alarm, \n             or invalid date components\n\nExample:\n    >>> set_alarm_at_specific_time("2024:12:25:08:00:00")\n    True  # Sets alarm for Christmas morning 2024 at 8 AM\n\nNotes:\n    - All components must be zero-padded (2 digits except year)\