2025-07-01 01:59:40,613 - DEBUG - Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/embeddings', 'files': None, 'post_parser': <function Embeddings.create.<locals>.parser at 0x30fbed900>, 'json_data': {'input': ['Iraq reopens airspace - Iraqi News: Iraq reopens airspace - Iraqi News Image 1: Iraqi News 3.   Iraq reopens airspace Iraq reopens airspace Image 2:  Iraq reopens airspace Baghdad (IraqiNews.com) – The Iraqi Civil Aviation Authority has announced the reopening of Iraqi airspace to all air traffic, following a thorough security assessment and coordination with both national and international agencies. The 12-day closure of Iraqi airspace began on June 13. The reopening of airspace follows yesterday’s Iranian strike on the Al-Udeid Air Base in Qatar, which had prompted several Gulf countries, including Iraq, to suspend air traffic. The reopening of its airspace signals cautious optimism toward regional stability, though concerns remain about potential spillover into Iraqi territory. Image 5: Iraqi News', 'Iraqi airspace reopens as regional tensions ease, flights resume across ...: Iraqi airspace reopens as regional tensions ease, flights resume across Kurdistan | World News – India TV Image 3: India TV News *   News *   News 1.   News Iraq has reopened its airspace after a 10-day closure due to the Israel-Iran conflict, allowing international flights to resume across the country and Kurdistan Region. Iraqi airspace is once again open to international flights, marking a key step toward restoring regional aviation stability after nearly two weeks of closure due to escalating conflict between Israel and Iran. Top News *   World News *   Entertainment News *   Sports News *   Tech News *   Business News *   Health News *   Bihar News *   Delhi News *   Haryana News *   UP News *   Chhattisgarh News *   Gujarat News *   Karnataka News *   Maharashtra News *   Rajasthan News *   Telangana News', 'Iraq Reopens Airspace to International Air Traffic: The Iraqi Civil Aviation Authority announced in a press release that it has reopened Iraqi airspace to air traffic following a comprehensive assessment of the security situation and coordination with relevant national and international authorities.', 'Iraqi airspace is partially reopening - airlive.net: The Iraqi News Agency (INA), citing Ministry spokesman Maytham Al-Safi, said that southern airspace was reopened after approval of competent aviation authorities. Iraqi Airways flight to Cairo and flydubai flight to Dubai left Basra Airport in South of Iraq. An Iraqi Airways flight is also on approach to Najaf from Mumbai.', 'Iraq Resumes Full Civil Aviation Operations - Iraq Business News: Iraq Resumes Full Civil Aviation Operations | Iraq Business News *   Iraq Business Guide *   List of International Oil Companies in Iraq *   List of Oil and Gas Fields in Iraq Image 2: Iraq Business NewsIraq Business NewsAll the latest business news from Iraq Iraq Resumes Full Civil Aviation Operations Iraq receives 3 new Search and Rescue (SAR) Vessels Image 5: Ahmed Mousa Jiyad Image 6: Ahmed Tabaqchali Sign Up © 2025 Iraq Business News. Get Business News from Iraq to your inbox. By submitting this form, you are consenting to receive marketing emails from: Iraq Business News, Iraq Business News Ltd, The Pump House, Coton Hill, Shrewsbury, Shropshire, SY1 2DP, GB, http://www.iraq-businessnews.co.uk. Emails are serviced by Constant Contact. Sign Up!', 'Airspace restrictions over Middle East hit airlines with higher costs ...: As geopolitical tensions rise in the Middle East, airlines are grappling with significant operational challenges, including longer flight routes, rising fuel costs, and increased passenger disruptions. This article explores the impact of airspace restrictions due to conflicts in Israel, Iran, Iraq, and beyond.', "Updated: What's Happening to Flights Across the Middle East Conflict ...: Middle East airspace closures after U.S. strikes on Iran force airlines, including U.S. carriers, to cancel and reroute flights. Air travel across the Middle East is facing its most severe disruption in years as escalating conflict triggered by U.S. military strikes on Iranian nuclear sites forces airlines to cancel or divert thousands of flights. “The situation is fluid,” a Singapore Airlines spokesperson told_CNBC_ after the carrier canceled multiple flights to Dubai. British Airways, Air France-KLM, Iberia, Finnair, Singapore Airlines, and Kazakhstan’s Air Astana all canceled services to Dubai and Doha—two of the Middle East’s busiest aviation hubs. “Several other flights are being delayed or rerouted as a result,” Air Arabia told _The Khaleej Times_, noting that passengers transiting through UAE airports to suspended destinations will not be accepted for travel until further notice.", 'Airspace Closure Over Iran, Israel, Iraq, Jordan: How It Will Impact Travel: Flights in the Middle East stand suspended or diverted in light of airspace closures over Iran, Israel, Iraq, and Jordan.', 'Middle East Airspace Closures Disrupt Global Flights and Travel Plans: In late June 2025, rising conflicts in the Middle East triggered airspace closures across multiple countries, including Qatar and Iran. These closures caused major airlines to cancel or reroute flights, leading to delays, higher costs, and widespread disruption for travelers worldwide. Monitoring flight status and travel advisories is essential to navigate ongoing disruptions safely.', "Disruption as airlines cancel flights and reroute planes to avoid ...: *   CNN10 Image 1: People stand in front of a flight information display screen showing information about delayed and canceled flights at Queen Alia International Airport in Amman, Jordan. Global air traffic has been disrupted following Israel’s strikes on Iran Friday, with several major airlines suspending flights to and from locations in the Middle East and rerouting their planes to avoid much of the region’s airspace. Israel, Iran and Jordan all closed their airspace in the wake of the attack, while Iran suspended all domestic and international flights, the country’s state-affiliated Fars news agency reported on Friday, citing the civil aviation authority. Image 4: Israel's Ben Gurion Airport is empty of passengers on Friday after all flights were canceled.", 'Iraqi airspace remains closed to all flights » Iraqi News Agency: Baghdad - INA The Iraqi Civil Aviation Authority announced today, Saturday, the extension of the ban on Iraqi airspace to all flights. The authority stated in a statement received by the Iraqi News Agency (INA), "The ban on Iraqi airspace to all incoming and outgoing flights has been extended', 'Iraq Reopens Airspace to International Air Traffic: The Iraqi Civil Aviation Authority (ICAA) has announced on Tuesday the reopening of Iraqi airspace to international air traffic following a comprehensive security assessment and coordination with national and international stakeholders.', 'Iraq reopens airspace - Iraqi News: Baghdad (IraqiNews.com) - The Iraqi Civil Aviation Authority has announced the reopening of Iraqi airspace to all air traffic, following a thorough security assessment and coordination with both', 'Iraqi airspace is partially reopening - airlive.net: The Iraqi News Agency (INA), citing Ministry spokesman Maytham Al-Safi, said that southern airspace was reopened after approval of competent aviation authorities. Iraqi Airways flight to Cairo and flydubai flight to Dubai left Basra Airport in South of Iraq. An Iraqi Airways flight is also on approach to Najaf from Mumbai.', 'Iraqi airspace reopens as regional tensions ease, flights resume across ...: Iraq has reopened its airspace after a 10-day closure due to the Israel-Iran conflict, allowing international flights to resume across the country and Kurdistan Region. The move follows a US', 'Iraq reopens airspace - Iraqi News: Iraq reopens airspace - Iraqi News Image 1: Iraqi News 3.   Iraq reopens airspace Iraq reopens airspace Image 2:  Iraq reopens airspace Baghdad (IraqiNews.com) – The Iraqi Civil Aviation Authority has announced the reopening of Iraqi airspace to all air traffic, following a thorough security assessment and coordination with both national and international agencies. The 12-day closure of Iraqi airspace began on June 13. The reopening of airspace follows yesterday’s Iranian strike on the Al-Udeid Air Base in Qatar, which had prompted several Gulf countries, including Iraq, to suspend air traffic. The reopening of its airspace signals cautious optimism toward regional stability, though concerns remain about potential spillover into Iraqi territory. Image 5: Iraqi News', 'Iraq Reopens Airspace to International Air Traffic: Baghdad, June 24 (QNA) - The Iraqi Civil Aviation Authority announced on Monday fully reopening its airspace to air traffic. The Iraqi Civil Aviation Authority announced in a press release that it has reopened Iraqi airspace to air traffic following a comprehensive assessment of the security situation and coordination with relevant national and international authorities. The press statement', 'Iraq Reopens Airspace to International Air Traffic: By John Lee. The Iraqi Civil Aviation Authority (ICAA) has announced on Tuesday the reopening of Iraqi airspace to international air traffic following a comprehensive security assessment and coordination with national and international stakeholders.', 'Iraqi airspace is partially reopening - airlive.net: The Iraqi News Agency (INA), citing Ministry spokesman Maytham Al-Safi, said that southern airspace was reopened after approval of competent aviation authorities. Iraqi Airways flight to Cairo and flydubai flight to Dubai left Basra Airport in South of Iraq. An Iraqi Airways flight is also on approach to Najaf from Mumbai.', 'Iraqi airspace reopens as regional tensions ease, flights resume across ...: Iraqi airspace reopens as regional tensions ease, flights resume across Kurdistan | World News – India TV Image 3: India TV News *   News *   News 1.   News Iraq has reopened its airspace after a 10-day closure due to the Israel-Iran conflict, allowing international flights to resume across the country and Kurdistan Region. Iraqi airspace is once again open to international flights, marking a key step toward restoring regional aviation stability after nearly two weeks of closure due to escalating conflict between Israel and Iran. Top News *   World News *   Entertainment News *   Sports News *   Tech News *   Business News *   Health News *   Bihar News *   Delhi News *   Haryana News *   UP News *   Chhattisgarh News *   Gujarat News *   Karnataka News *   Maharashtra News *   Rajasthan News *   Telangana News', 'Iraqi airspace reopens as regional tensions ease, flights resume across ...: Iraqi airspace reopens as regional tensions ease, flights resume across Kurdistan | World News – India TV Image 3: India TV News *   News *   News 1.   News Iraq has reopened its airspace after a 10-day closure due to the Israel-Iran conflict, allowing international flights to resume across the country and Kurdistan Region. Iraqi airspace is once again open to international flights, marking a key step toward restoring regional aviation stability after nearly two weeks of closure due to escalating conflict between Israel and Iran. Top News *   World News *   Entertainment News *   Sports News *   Tech News *   Business News *   Health News *   Bihar News *   Delhi News *   Haryana News *   UP News *   Chhattisgarh News *   Gujarat News *   Karnataka News *   Maharashtra News *   Rajasthan News *   Telangana News', 'Iraq reopens airspace - Iraqi News: Iraq reopens airspace - Iraqi News Image 1: Iraqi News 3.   Iraq reopens airspace Iraq reopens airspace Image 2:  Iraq reopens airspace Baghdad (IraqiNews.com) – The Iraqi Civil Aviation Authority has announced the reopening of Iraqi airspace to all air traffic, following a thorough security assessment and coordination with both national and international agencies. The 12-day closure of Iraqi airspace began on June 13. The reopening of airspace follows yesterday’s Iranian strike on the Al-Udeid Air Base in Qatar, which had prompted several Gulf countries, including Iraq, to suspend air traffic. The reopening of its airspace signals cautious optimism toward regional stability, though concerns remain about potential spillover into Iraqi territory. Image 5: Iraqi News', "Iraq reopens airspace as Middle East situation improves: He added that reopening Iraqi airspace will enhance Iraq's strategic geographic position as an air corridor connecting East and West, and will help reduce flight time and fuel costs for global airlines. Iraq closed its airspace to international air traffic following the outbreak of the Israel-Iran conflict on June 13. (Xinhua/NAN)", "Flights resume at Iraqi Kurdistan airports after airspace reopening: The reopening followed a ceasefire agreement brokered by U.S. President Donald Trump, signaling a de-escalation in the conflict. Iraq's transport ministry stated that flights are now considered safe over Iraqi and Kurdish airspace.", "Iraq Reopens Airspace to International Air Traffic: The reopening is expected to strengthen Iraq's strategic geographic position as an east-west air corridor, helping global airlines reduce flight times and fuel costs."], 'model': 'text-embedding-ada-002', 'encoding_format': 'base64'}}
