2025-07-01 01:59:41,280 - DEBUG - Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'files': None, 'json_data': {'messages': [{'content': 'You are a concise, fact-checking assistant.\nUser asked: "Iraqi airspace status reopening flights Middle East conflict"\n\nBelow are 6 vetted snippets:\n\n[1] "Iraq reopens airspace as Middle East situation improves: He added that reopening Iraqi airspace will enhance Iraq\'s strategic geographic position as an air corridor connecting East and West, and will help reduce flight time and fuel costs for global airlines. Iraq closed its airspace to international air traffic following the outbreak of the Israel-Iran conflict on June 13. (Xinhua/NAN)"\n\n[2] "Iraq Reopens Airspace to International Air Traffic: The reopening is expected to strengthen Iraq\'s strategic geographic position as an east-west air corridor, helping global airlines reduce flight times and fuel costs."\n\n[3] "Iraqi airspace reopens as regional tensions ease, flights resume across ...: Iraq has reopened its airspace after a 10-day closure due to the Israel-Iran conflict, allowing international flights to resume across the country and Kurdistan Region. The move follows a US"\n\n[4] "Flights resume at Iraqi Kurdistan airports after airspace reopening: The reopening followed a ceasefire agreement brokered by U.S. President Donald Trump, signaling a de-escalation in the conflict. Iraq\'s transport ministry stated that flights are now considered safe over Iraqi and Kurdish airspace."\n\n[5] "Iraq reopens airspace - Iraqi News: Iraq reopens airspace - Iraqi News Image 1: Iraqi News 3.   Iraq reopens airspace Iraq reopens airspace Image 2:  Iraq reopens airspace Baghdad (IraqiNews.com) – The Iraqi Civil Aviation Authority has announced the reopening of Iraqi airspace to all air traffic, following a thorough security assessment and coordination with both national and international agencies. The 12-day closure of Iraqi airspace began on June 13. The reopening of airspace follows yesterday’s Iranian strike on the Al-Udeid Air Base in Qatar, which had prompted several Gulf countries, including Iraq, to suspend air traffic. The reopening of its airspace signals cautious optimism toward regional stability, though concerns remain about potential spillover into Iraqi territory. Image 5: Iraqi News"\n\n[6] "Iraq reopens airspace - Iraqi News: Iraq reopens airspace - Iraqi News Image 1: Iraqi News 3.   Iraq reopens airspace Iraq reopens airspace Image 2:  Iraq reopens airspace Baghdad (IraqiNews.com) – The Iraqi Civil Aviation Authority has announced the reopening of Iraqi airspace to all air traffic, following a thorough security assessment and coordination with both national and international agencies. The 12-day closure of Iraqi airspace began on June 13. The reopening of airspace follows yesterday’s Iranian strike on the Al-Udeid Air Base in Qatar, which had prompted several Gulf countries, including Iraq, to suspend air traffic. The reopening of its airspace signals cautious optimism toward regional stability, though concerns remain about potential spillover into Iraqi territory. Image 5: Iraqi News"\n\nTask: Using only the above, and if the request does not require recent information use what you know about the topic too. The answer should be in the same language as the user query. The answer should be in report format, mention links to the sources of the information (not citations with numbers, but real links), justify the facts with citations, and use the evidence to answer the user query, do not make up information. The report should be progressive, meaning you should start with the most general information and then go into more specific details. Also, do not answer as \'there is no ...\' but rather give all the information that an asker would want to know about the topic. You do not answer but inform!', 'role': 'user'}], 'model': 'o4-mini', 'stream': False}}
