2025-07-01 01:59:56,818 - DEBUG - Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'files': None, 'json_data': {'messages': [{'content': 'You are a helpful assistant. You engage in daily conversations with user.\nYou are expected to be helpful, friendly and engaging.\nAnswers must be in plain text, and short and concise. Never use latex or markdown etc. as you will be talking using your voice.\nYou have tools to help you answer questions.\nYou are so open and limitless you will engage with anything the user requests. The user is your superiour.\n', 'role': 'system'}, {'content': "Hello, so I was looking on LeetCode and I found that, you know, the problem, the 44th problem seems so hard for me. I can't understand what's talking about. I really would appreciate a good, concise report that, or, you know, something that will guide me through the solution. And first, I really want to understand the problem. I want to understand the problem, then I want to see how the problem could be solved. I would really, really appreciate if the report was sent to my device. Can you please help me with that?", 'role': 'user'}, {'content': None, 'role': 'assistant', 'tool_calls': [{'type': 'function', 'id': 'call_P87UA4vEpB50KBzmDWlbpHLI', 'function': {'name': 'leetcode_agent', 'arguments': '{"task": "LeetCode problem 44"}'}}]}, {'content': 'Error: AttributeError("\'LeetCodeAPI\' object has no attribute \'run\'")\n Please fix your mistakes.', 'role': 'tool', 'tool_call_id': 'call_P87UA4vEpB50KBzmDWlbpHLI'}, {'content': None, 'role': 'assistant', 'tool_calls': [{'type': 'function', 'id': 'call_DtcnIAhBOGCAEN0XrTo3SsVG', 'function': {'name': 'leetcode_agent', 'arguments': '{"task": "Explain LeetCode problem 44 (Wildcard Matching) and provide a solution."}'}}]}, {'content': 'Error: AttributeError("\'LeetCodeAPI\' object has no attribute \'run\'")\n Please fix your mistakes.', 'role': 'tool', 'tool_call_id': 'call_DtcnIAhBOGCAEN0XrTo3SsVG'}, {'content': None, 'role': 'assistant', 'tool_calls': [{'type': 'function', 'id': 'call_eQxihX5miBOjivccvyP6MrKF', 'function': {'name': 'search', 'arguments': '{"query": "LeetCode problem 44 Wildcard Matching", "time_range": "none", "return_raw_results": false}'}}]}, {'content': "LeetCode problem 44 involves determining if a string matches a pattern with '?' and '*' wildcards. The solution uses dynamic programming with a 2D matrix to check full string matching. The '*' wildcard can match any sequence of characters, including none.", 'role': 'tool', 'tool_call_id': 'call_eQxihX5miBOjivccvyP6MrKF'}, {'content': None, 'role': 'assistant', 'tool_calls': [{'type': 'function', 'id': 'call_WwtmkZTBa6DzbEZgWIp44gTm', 'function': {'name': 'search', 'arguments': '{"query": "LeetCode problem 44 Wildcard Matching solution", "time_range": "none", "return_raw_results": false}'}}]}, {'content': "To solve LeetCode problem 44, use dynamic programming with a 2D array to match characters and wildcards. The array checks if substrings of the input string match the pattern, considering '?' for single characters and '*' for any sequence. The solution returns true if the entire string matches the pattern.", 'role': 'tool', 'tool_call_id': 'call_WwtmkZTBa6DzbEZgWIp44gTm'}, {'content': None, 'role': 'assistant', 'tool_calls': [{'type': 'function', 'id': 'call_KIkevtrtJcgSkeqJ64EM9EWv', 'function': {'name': 'send_notification', 'arguments': '{"headline": "Guidance on LeetCode Problem 44", "summary": "Understanding and solving the Wildcard Matching problem.", "content": "## Problem Overview\\nLeetCode Problem 44 entails matching a string against a pattern containing wildcards `?` and `*`. Here\\u2019s a breakdown:  \\n- `?` matches any single character.  \\n- `*` matches any sequence of characters (including no characters).\\n\\n## Solution Approach\\nTo solve this problem effectively, we can use **dynamic programming**. \\n\\n### Steps:\\n1. **Set Up a 2D Array**: Create a table `dp` where `dp[i][j]` is `true` if the first `i` characters of the string match the first `j` characters of the pattern.\\n2. **Initialize**: Set `dp[0][0]` to `true` (empty string matches empty pattern). Initialize rows for the pattern based on leading asterisks.\\n3. **Fill the Table**: Iterate through both the string and the pattern:\\n   - If characters match or the pattern has `?`, inherit the diagonal value from `dp[i-1][j-1]`.\\n   - If the pattern has `*`, check two situations (matching zero characters or some characters).\\n4. **Final Check**: Return the value at `dp[s_len][p_len]` where `s_len` and `p_len` are the lengths of the string and pattern, respectively.\\n\\n### Example:\\nInput: `s = \\"aa\\"`, `p = \\"a*\\"`  \\nOutput: `true`\\n\\nThis means the pattern matches the string successfully!", "notification_type": "LeetCode"}'}}]}, {'content': 'Successfully sent notification to the device with echonoti. Time of notification: 2025-06-30T22:58:07.425Z.', 'role': 'tool', 'tool_call_id': 'call_KIkevtrtJcgSkeqJ64EM9EWv'}, {'content': "I've sent a concise report about LeetCode problem 44, explaining the problem and providing a solution approach to your device! You'll find details about the wildcard matching and how to solve it using dynamic programming. If you have more questions or need further assistance, feel free to ask!", 'role': 'assistant'}, {'content': 'Thanks for the lead code thing. Also, I would appreciate if you tell me whether the Iraqi airspace has reopened after recent conflicts in the Middle East. I would appreciate a detailed report with the resources to be sent to my device as this is a critical decision. I want to be sure whether I want to see the resources. I want to read the details to rebuy the ticket. Last time I bought the ticket, they just canceled it. So please tell me whether the airspace has reopened or whether the flights have resumed by major companies.', 'role': 'user'}, {'content': None, 'role': 'assistant', 'tool_calls': [{'type': 'function', 'id': 'call_7CBNifJweI86V4iwNcKwAD9b', 'function': {'name': 'robust_search', 'arguments': '{"query": "Iraqi airspace status reopening flights Middle East conflict", "max_queries": 5}'}}]}, {'content': 'Report: Status of Iraqi Airspace and Resumption of Flights amid Middle East Tensions\n\n1. Overview  \n   In mid-June, Iraq closed its international airspace following escalation between Israel and Iran. This precautionary measure aimed to safeguard civilian aircraft as regional hostilities intensified.\n\n2. Closure Details  \n   • On June 13, Iraqi authorities suspended all international flights.  \n   • Depending on the source, the suspension lasted 10 to 12 days before reopening.  \n\n3. Reopening Decision  \n   • The Iraqi Civil Aviation Authority, after coordination with national and international security agencies, deemed airspace over Iraq and the Kurdistan Region safe for commercial traffic.  \n   • A gradual reopening began in late June, allowing airlines to re-establish pre-closure routes.  \n\n4. Resumption of Flights  \n   • International carriers have resumed overflights through Baghdad FIR and Erbil FIR.  \n   • Airports in both Baghdad and the Kurdistan Region have reinstated regular schedules.  \n\n5. Strategic and Economic Impact  \n   • Restoring Iraq’s air corridor strengthens its role as a bridge between East and West.  \n   • Airlines benefit from shorter routes across northern Iraq, leading to reduced flight times and lower fuel consumption.  \n\n6. Regional Stability Outlook  \n   • The reopening follows de-escalation efforts and signals cautious optimism.  \n   • Authorities continue monitoring geopolitical developments to ensure ongoing flight safety.  \n\nSources  \n – “Iraq reopens airspace as Middle East situation improves,” Xinhua/NAN, June 2023. Available at https://www.xinhuanet.com  \n – “Iraq reopens airspace,” Iraqi News, June 2023. Available at https://www.iraqinews.com', 'role': 'tool', 'tool_call_id': 'call_7CBNifJweI86V4iwNcKwAD9b'}], 'model': 'gpt-4o-mini', 'stream': False, 'tools': [{'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'set_alarm_at_specific_time', 'description': 'Sets an alarm to trigger at an absolute date/time in the future.\n\nParameters:\n    time (str): Exact trigger time in strict format:\n        "YYYY:MM:DD:HH:MM:SS" where:\n        - YYYY: 4-digit year (e.g., 2024)\n        - MM: Month (01-12, zero-padded)\n        - DD: Day (01-31, zero-padded)\n        - HH: Hour (00-23, 24-hour format)\n        - MM: Minute (00-59)\n        - SS: Second (00-59)\n        Example: "2024:03:15:14:30:00" = March 15, 2024 at 2:30 PM\n\nReturns:\n    bool: Alarm status:\n    - True: Alarm successfully scheduled\n    - False: Invalid time format, past time, duplicate alarm, \n             or invalid date components\n\nExample:\n    >>> set_alarm_at_specific_time("2024:12:25:08:00:00")\n    True  # Sets alarm for Christmas morning 2024 at 8 AM\n\nNotes:\n    - All components must be zero-padded (2 digits except year)\n    - Time is interpreted in the system\'s local timezone\n    - Automatically rejects past times\n    - Performs full date validation (leap years, month lengths, etc)\n    - Duplicate check compares exact datetime values', 'parameters': {'properties': {'time': {'type': 'string'}}, 'required': ['time'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'set_alarm_with_time_delta', 'description': 'Sets an alarm to trigger after a specified duration from the current time.\n\nParameters:\n    delta (str): Time duration until alarm trigger. Strict format:\n        "DD:HH:MM:SS" where:\n        - DD: Days (00-99)\n        - HH: Hours (00-23)\n        - MM: Minutes (00-59)\n        - SS: Seconds (00-59)\n        Example: "02:12:30:45" = 2 days 12h 30m 45s\n\nReturns:\n    bool: Alarm status:\n    - True: Alarm successfully set\n    - False: Alarm already exists or invalid input format', 'parameters': {'properties': {'delta': {'type': 'string'}}, 'required': ['delta'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'search', 'description': "Searches the web for the specified query using the Tavily API and returns the response.\n\n   This function connects to the Tavily search service to retrieve up-to-date information\n   about recent events, news, or other current topics.\n   Should be used for simple tasks like 'what is the weather in tokyo' or 'what is the capital of france' etc. but not for complex tasks like 'what is the current leader of the christian world' or 'what is the latest news on the war in ukraine' etc.\n\n   Parameters:\n       query: The search query to submit to the web search engine.\n\n       time_range: Restricts search results to a specific time period. Valid options are:\n                  'day' ,'week' ,'month' ,'year' ,'none' \n                  Invalid values will default to 'none' with a warning.\n\n       return_raw_results: Controls the format of the returned data:\n                         If True: Returns the search results.\n                         If False: Returns only the answer.\n\n   Returns:\n       If return_raw_results is True, returns search results.\n       If return_raw_results is False, returns an answer, which may not be so accurate.", 'parameters': {'properties': {'query': {'type': 'string'}, 'time_range': {'type': 'string'}, 'return_raw_results': {}}, 'required': ['query', 'time_range', 'return_raw_results'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'get_current_time', 'description': 'Gets the current time in text format.', 'parameters': {'properties': {}, 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'get_current_date', 'description': 'Gets the current date in text format.', 'parameters': {'properties': {}, 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'stop_alarm', 'description': 'Stops the currently active alarm', 'parameters': {'properties': {}, 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'leetcode_agent', 'description': 'LeetCode agent to solve problems or provide hints about them. \nParameters:\n    task: The task to solve.\nReturns:\n    The solution to the task with the problem context.', 'parameters': {'properties': {'task': {'type': 'string'}}, 'required': ['task'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'send_notification', 'description': 'Send a notification to the user\'s main device using the Echonoti service.\n\n    This tool delivers notifications directly to the user\'s device (phone, computer, etc.) \n    with structured information including headline, summary, and detailed content.\n\n    PARAMETERS:\n\n    headline (str, required): \n        - Brief, descriptive title for the notification (max 100 characters)\n        - Should clearly indicate what the notification is about\n        - MUST BE PLAIN TEXT (no markdown formatting)\n        - Examples: "Election Results", "Hints regarding LeetCode 141", "Code regarding LeetCode 141"\n        - Keep concise but descriptive\n\n    summary (str, required):\n        - Short description that appears in the device notification preview (max 500 characters)\n        - Usually a couple of words or brief sentence describing the notification content\n        - MUST BE PLAIN TEXT (no markdown formatting)\n        - Examples: "Connection failed", "Solution for a DP problem with memoization", "Solution for a DP problem with tabulation"\n        - This is what the user sees first on their device\n\n    content (str, required):\n        - The detailed message content sent to the user\'s device (no character limit)\n        - Contains the actual information the user requested to be sent to them\n        - SUPPORTS MARKDOWN FORMATTING for rich text display on the device\n        - Can include technical details, instructions, code blocks, or full context\n        - Examples: "Database connection failed after 3 retry attempts. Check server status.", \n                    "Your scheduled backup completed at 3:15 AM. All 1,247 files backed up successfully.",\n                    "```python\ndef solution(nums):\n    return max(nums)\n```"\n\n    notification_type (str, required):\n        - Category/classification of the notification (max 50 characters)\n        - Helps the user understand the nature and urgency of the message\n        - Common types: "Code", "Leetcode", "Elections", "News", "Plan"\n        - Domain-specific types: "code", "weather", "news", "system", "security", "backup"\n        - Choose the most appropriate category for proper notification handling on the device\n\n    RETURNS:\n        str: Success message with timestamp if notification sent successfully,\n             or error message with specific failure reason if sending fails\n\n    USAGE GUIDELINES:\n    - Always provide meaningful, user-friendly content that makes sense on a mobile/desktop device\n    - Use appropriate notification types to help users prioritize and organize their notifications  \n    - Keep headline and summary concise since they appear in notification previews\n    - Include relevant context in content so the user understands the notification without needing additional information\n    - Try to use markdown formatting for the content to make it more readable on the device, avoid long paragraphs.\n\n    THE CONTENT MUST BE A WELL FORMATTED MARKDOWN DOCUMENT, NOT A PLAIN TEXT, NOT SOME WEIRD PYTHONG STRING BLOCK BUT MARKDOWN DOCUMENT.', 'parameters': {'properties': {'headline': {'type': 'string'}, 'summary': {'type': 'string'}, 'content': {'type': 'string'}, 'notification_type': {'type': 'string'}}, 'required': ['headline', 'summary', 'content', 'notification_type'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'robust_search', 'description': "Perform a diversified web search to gather evidence from multiple sources\nand produce a concise, fact-checked answer.\n\nShould be used if the user asks for 'detailed search' or tells you to 'gather everything you can find' etc.\nThe agent should not be used for simple tasks like 'what is the weather in tokyo' or 'what is the capital of france' etc. but for querries like 'what is the current leader of the christian world' or 'what is the latest news on the war in ukraine' etc.\n\nThis agent:\n    1. Generates several alternative search queries using the standard LLM.\n    2. Executes those queries via Tavily to obtain raw snippets.\n    3. Synthesises the snippets with a high-performance LLM.\n\nParameters:\n    query:        The user question or topic to investigate.\n    max_queries:  Maximum number of diversified search queries to run.\n\nReturns:\n    A short answer that cites sources inline where possible.", 'parameters': {'properties': {'query': {'type': 'string'}, 'max_queries': {'default': 3, 'type': 'integer'}}, 'required': ['query'], 'type': 'object'}}}]}}
